<title>UK: Lucasvarity acquires new friction business.</title>
<headline>Lucasvarity acquires new friction business.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Engineering group LucasVarity said on Friday that it had acquired a friction manufacturing business for its aftermarket division.</p>
<p>The business, owned by a group of manufacturers in Spain and U.S. make brake friction materials under the brand name 'Remsa'.</p>
<p>The company did not mention the consideration paid for the business which had a net asset value, excluding cash of 19 million stg.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
